  1password-token             'ops_eyJ([A-Za-z0-9+_-]|\\?/){100,}={0,3}|A3-[A-Z0-9]{6}-([A-Z0-9]{11}|[A-Z0-9]{6}-[A-Z0-9]{5})-[A-Z0-9]{5}-[A-Z0-9]{5}-[A-Z0-9]{5}'  # gitleaks: 1password-service-account-token, 1password-secret-key
  # source: developers.facebook.com/documentation/facebook-login/guides/access-tokens (opaque, EAAC by example).
  # The fourth character stays M or C, though Meta fixes none: any other let
  # base64 image data in a real SVG read as 30 tokens, 5 past the stand-in
  # test (v0.12.0), since `EAA` is how base64 writes 0x10 and zero bytes.
  # An app access token is the app id, `|` and the app secret ("access_token={your-app_id}|{your-app_secret}", the same page); the
  # secret's length is unstated, and 24 keeps ids joined by `|` to a name out.
  # A left edge on EAA, as alibaba-access-key-id's: base64 image data in two
  # SVGs inside a zip read as tokens (v0.29.0, measured by --archives).
  facebook-token              '(^|[^A-Za-z0-9+/]|\\[a-z]|\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4}|\\x[0-9A-Fa-f]{2}|%[0-9A-Fa-f]{2})EAA[MC][A-Za-z0-9]{100,}|[0-9]{13,20}\|[A-Za-z0-9]{24,}'  # gitleaks: facebook-page-access-token
  # source: developer.squareup.com/reference/square/oauth-api/obtain-token (sq0csp-, by example); developer.squareup.com/docs/oauth-api/receive-and-manage-tokens (an access token, EAAA and 60 of [A-Za-z0-9_], by example, and "don't use token length for validation": 60 or more)
  # EAAA takes alibaba-access-key-id's left edge: base64 holds it often.
  square-token                'sq0(atp|csp)-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22,}|(^|[^A-Za-z0-9+/]|\\[a-z]|\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4}|\\x[0-9A-Fa-f]{2}|%[0-9A-Fa-f]{2})EAAA[A-Za-z0-9_-]{60,}'  # gitleaks: square-access-token
  # source: pulumi.com/registry/packages/pulumiservice/api-docs/api/tokens/personaltoken/ (pul-)
